From: smolvm <noreply@smolmachines.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fuse: let a submount be idmapped when its parent can be

A FUSE superblock starts with SB_I_NOIDMAP, and the server's init reply clears
it when the server allows idmapped mounts. A submount gets a superblock of its
own that never sees an init reply, so it refuses idmapped mounts forever, even
on a connection that allows them: mount_setattr(MOUNT_ATTR_IDMAP) fails with
EINVAL for any directory virtio-fs announces as a submount (a host directory on
another filesystem than its share's root). Inherit the parent's state instead.
---
--- a/fs/fuse/inode.c
+++ b/fs/fuse/inode.c
@@ -1736,6 +1736,15 @@
 	if (parent_sb->s_subtype && !sb->s_subtype)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/*
+	 * fuse_sb_defaults() refuses idmapped mounts until the server allows them
+	 * in its init reply, and only the connection's first superblock sees that
+	 * reply. A submount shares the connection, so it allows them when its
+	 * parent does.
+	 */
+	if (!(parent_sb->s_iflags & SB_I_NOIDMAP))
+		sb->s_iflags &= ~SB_I_NOIDMAP;
+
 	fuse_fill_attr_from_inode(&root_attr, parent_fi);
 	root = fuse_iget(sb, parent_fi->nodeid, 0, &root_attr, 0, 0,
 			 fuse_get_evict_ctr(fm->fc));
